audio.cpp fork delta: a fused bf16 rounding unary op plus f16<->bf16 copy
pipelines, captured 2026-09-23 (previously untracked in external/ggml - see
0008's header for why that matters). Source commits: audio.cpp #393 (ff38f154,
Breeze-TTS 2 weight packing + fused bf16 rounding) and #431 (8a9cb757, Breeze
encoder chunked VRAM).

  - GGML_UNARY_OP_ROUND_BF16 / ggml_round_bf16(ctx, a): rounds every element to
    bf16 precision and keeps it in f32 - the same values as an f32 -> bf16 ->
    f32 cast pair, as one node and without the bf16 intermediate. Appended at
    the tail of ggml_unary_op so existing values do not move.
      CPU   : ops.cpp dispatch + unary-ops.{h,cpp}.
      CUDA  : unary.{cu,cuh}, contiguous and strided kernels, dispatched and
              advertised from ggml-cuda.cu.
      Vulkan: round_bf16.comp / round_bf16_strided.comp for f32/f16/bf16 input.
  - Vulkan cpy/contig_cpy pipelines for f16 -> bf16 and bf16 -> f16 (the
    backend only had f32 <-> bf16). The copy shaders' bf16 read is split into a
    named temporary so the bf16 -> f16 variant compiles.

Consumers: families that emulate bf16 checkpoints on f32 compute (Breeze-TTS 2,
the Breeze ASR encoder). Retire when upstream ggml gains an equivalent op.

Rebased onto ggml 0.24.0 (456172ec) on 2026-09-23: upstream registers its
new fused unary-mul pipelines (CREATE_UNARY_MUL) where this patch registers
the round_bf16 pipelines in ggml_vk_load_shaders; both are kept.

